winewayland: end an open menu when the focus leaves the application

Operator: "the dropdowns are also persisting on the top of everything when switching between apps" (Lightroom
Classic, his prefix and the clean room). On Windows, switching apps closes an open menu. Our focus-leave handler
(deactivate-on-focus-leave) sends WM_CANCELMODE to the foreground window, and DefWindowProc's end_menu() only ends a
menu owned by that window. Lightroom Classic shows its panel dropdowns (Metadata view and preset, etc.) as popup
menus owned by the ComboBox child control (+menu: TrackPopupMenuEx hwnd = a ComboBox, not the AgWinMainFrame), so
they stayed open, drawn above the app the user switched to. Menu-bar menus (owned by the frame) already closed.

When the keyboard focus has left the process and this thread is in menu mode (GetGUIThreadInfo GUI_INMENUMODE),
the handler now calls NtUserEndMenu(), which ends the menu whatever owns it, as EndMenu does. It runs before the
"still the foreground window?" check, so it also applies when the focus went to another Wine process.
Kill switch NEUTRON_DEACT_ENDMENU=0.

Verified on a nested KWin (clean-room LrcRelease, runtime 122 + this driver), switching to KCalc with each open:
Library menu (closed before and after), Metadata view dropdown and Metadata preset dropdown (stayed open on 122;
close with this). Known-bad: NEUTRON_DEACT_ENDMENU=0 leaves the view dropdown open. Harness:
preserved-fixes/harnesses/kwin-nested/ (start.sh, place.sh, activate.sh) + menucmd.exe (click, info, postmsg).

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -458,6 +458,14 @@
     return on;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON: kill switch for ending an open menu when focus leaves the process (see WM_WAYLAND_KILL_FOREGROUND). */
+static BOOL neutron_deact_endmenu(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) on = neutron_gate("NEUTRON_DEACT_ENDMENU", TRUE);
+    return on;
+}
+
 static BOOL neutron_gate_deactivate_on_leave(void)
 {
     static int on = -1;
@@ -1827,6 +1835,24 @@
             return 0;
         }
 
+        /* NEUTRON: an open menu ends when its application loses the focus, whatever window owns it,
+         * as on Windows. The WM_CANCELMODE below only ends a menu owned by the window it is sent to
+         * (end_menu), and Lightroom Classic shows its panel dropdowns as popup menus owned by the
+         * ComboBox child control (TrackPopupMenuEx hwnd = the ComboBox), not its main frame: switching
+         * apps left them open, drawn above every other window.
+         * Done before the foreground check, so it also runs when the focus went to another Wine
+         * process, whose window is already the foreground one. Kill switch NEUTRON_DEACT_ENDMENU=0. */
+        if (neutron_deact_endmenu())
+        {
+            GUITHREADINFO info = {.cbSize = sizeof(info)};
+
+            if (NtUserGetGUIThreadInfo(GetCurrentThreadId(), &info) && (info.flags & GUI_INMENUMODE))
+            {
+                ERR("neutron-wlkillfg: hwnd=%p ending the open menu (owner %p)\n", hwnd, info.hwndMenuOwner);
+                NtUserEndMenu();
+            }
+        }
+
         /* Messages sent below may themselves change the foreground window, so re-check rather
          * than trusting the state we saw when the leave arrived. */
         if (hwnd != NtUserGetForegroundWindow()) return 0;
